{
  "_note": "How each section is played (docs/power-chord-engine-brief.md §6). `register`: low = the key's lowest comfortable zone (open strings when the key has them), lift = chorusLift frets higher (engine-settings.json). `shapes`: voicing-shapes.json ids the path search may use. `rhythms`: per feel, a list of variants; seed 0 plays the first, regenerate cycles through them. Rhythm cells, 8 per bar (eighth notes): D = downstroke, U = upstroke, x = dead strum, - = let the last hit ring, . = rest. `articulation` per bar (cycled): pm = palm-muted, ring = let ring. `accents`: accented cells in every bar. `pushes`: bars whose last cell plays the next bar's chord an eighth early. `stopBar`: a full-band stop after that bar's first hit (N.C.).",
  "library": {
    "_note": "The voicing shown on chord chips (Chords page, Power Chords panel) and played by their play buttons (with the feel's strum from rhythm-patterns.json): compact 2-note shapes in the low/mid zone.",
    "register": "low",
    "openStrings": false,
    "shapes": ["E2", "A2", "D2"]
  },
  "sections": {
